        // and the fallback increments depositsCount in the reference behavior only when owner calls). We must read c's public getter.
        // We express the universal property as: for any non-owner caller and any inputs, depositsCount == 0 after the attempt.
        if (caller != address(this)) {
            assertTrue(after == 0);
        } else {
